  <main class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <h1 class="section-title">Cron Jobs: Scheduling Tasks Like a Pro</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:24px;">Published: August 10, 2026</p>
      <article style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.8;">
        <p>Cron is a time-based job scheduler in Unix-like operating systems. It enables you to run commands or scripts automatically at specified intervals — from every minute to once a year.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">The Cron Expression</h2>
        <p>A standard cron expression has 5 fields: minute (0-59), hour (0-23), day of month (1-31), month (1-12), and day of week (0-6, where 0 is Sunday). Each field can be a specific value, a range (1-5), a list (1,3,5), or <code>*</code> (any).</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Common Examples</h2>
        <p><code>0 * * * *</code> — every hour at minute 0. <code>0 0 * * *</code> — every day at midnight. <code>0 0 * * 0</code> — every Sunday at midnight. <code>*/15 * * * *</code> — every 15 minutes.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Best Practices</h2>
        <p>Log output to a file for debugging. Use absolute paths in scripts. Test with <code>run-parts</code> before scheduling. Consider timezone differences if your server runs UTC. Use monitoring to ensure jobs actually run.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Beyond System Cron</h2>
        <p>Modern applications often use distributed schedulers like Airflow, Prefect, or cloud-native solutions (AWS EventBridge, GCP Cloud Scheduler). These offer better visibility, retries, and monitoring than traditional cron.</p>
      </article>

      <div style="margin-top:32px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);">
