      <section class="faq" style="margin-top:32px;">
        <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
        <details>
          <summary>What's the difference between cron and at?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Cron is for recurring jobs. <code>at</code> is for one-time scheduled tasks.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use environment variables in cron?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Yes, but cron has a minimal environment. Define variables at the top of your crontab or source your profile in the script.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What if two cron jobs overlap?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Use lock files (e.g., <code>flock</code>) to prevent concurrent execution of the same job.</div>
        </details>
      </section>
